# A2ML Profile: a2ml/agentic

@abstract:
Validation profile for the 6a2 AGENTIC.a2ml metadata record (AI-agent
interaction patterns, permissions, and constraints). Non-executable;
five-axis-bounded per SPEC.adoc Section 8.2.
@end

@profile-def(id=a2ml/agentic, version="1.0.0"):
required_sections:
  - metadata
  - agent-permissions
  - agent-constraints
allowed_directives: closed [ profile ]
required_directives: []
reference_classes: []
min_attestation: checked
@end

# Notes

@rationale:
AGENTIC governs what automated agents may do in the repo. Both
`agent-permissions` (the allow side) and `agent-constraints` (the deny side)
are required: an AGENTIC record that states permissions without constraints,
or vice versa, is dangerously half-specified. `maintenance-integrity` and
`automation-hooks` remain optional refinements.
@end
